  "implemented": [
    "The two retained preference commands have exact empty/boolean DTOs and defined boolean results. Source uses the existing DatabaseManager setting writer without new events, paths, window actions or session starts/stops.",
    "A captured optional native tray launch capability binds actual database/AgentManager owners. Public operations require a trusted current engine/document and separate dynamic global read/write grants. Source verifies a native document snapshot before dispatch; native fences ingress and final delivery. Hydration permits the read and fences the write.",
    "App-owned CloseRequested queries a distinct finite private boolean lookup under actual Source owner.run, without fabricating renderer identity. Bounded scalar SQL treats only exact stored text true as enabled, including huge malformed legacy settings without full getters/secret projection.",
    "Linux builds a real Tauri tray with fixed Open/Quit menu actions and a private exclusive0700 icon directory. Building an icon describes owned capability, not panel visibility. One per-App reservation bounds an unavoidable global listener with only a weak owner capture.",
    "Native CloseRequested preserves the main window while one retained preference decision runs. False enters existing owned application shutdown; true hides only the current physical main after async exact unique watcher/registered-host/unique-owner recheck. Raw GVariant type/byte bounds precede Rust projection.",
    "Missing or changed registered tray host leaves main visible/focused and presents one owned nonblocking local message. Fixed Open/ Quit remain native app actions across Source failure; failed Source close lookup uses normal owned application shutdown.",
    "Accepted close/menu/GIO work remains owned until actual callback retirement. Shutdown revokes admission/UI synchronously, joins raw work, independently retires tray/menu/dialog and exact icon-directory resources before Source profile release. Failed cleanup retains resources for explicit retry.",
    "No Source task action dispatcher, generic native menu payload, arbitrary setting writer or synthetic successful OS effect is added."
  ],
